@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### ====================================================================
### 1. STUDENTS CONTROLLER
### ====================================================================

### 1.1 GET /api/students — Success: 200 OK (Get all students)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.2 GET /api/students/{id} — Success: 200 OK (Get student by ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.3 GET /api/students/{id} — Failure: 404 Not Found (Non-existent student ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students/999
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.4 GET /api/students/search?name= — Success: 200 OK (Partial match search)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students/search?name=Ali
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.5 POST /api/students — Success: 201 Created (Create new student)
# Note: First run returns 201 (Created). Running it again returns 409 Conflict (duplicate email).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ziad Tarek",
  "email": "ziad.tarek@university.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2003-04-15T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.6 POST /api/students — Failure: 400 Bad Request (Validation failure - invalid email & empty name)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "invalid-email-format",
  "dateOfBirth": "2003-04-15T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.7 POST /api/students — Failure: 409 Conflict (Duplicate email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Another Ali",
  "email": "ali.mohamed@university.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.8 PUT /api/students/{id} — Success: 204 No Content (Update student)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/students/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ali Mohamed Updated",
  "email": "ali.mohamed@university.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2000-05-14T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.9 PUT /api/students/{id} — Failure: 404 Not Found (Update non-existent student)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/students/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ghost Student",
  "email": "ghost@university.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.10 PUT /api/students/{id} — Failure: 409 Conflict (Email in use by another student)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/students/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ali Mohamed",
  "email": "sara.ahmed@university.edu",
  "dateOfBirth": "2000-05-14T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 1.11 GET /api/students/{id}/courses — Success: 200 OK (Courses with grades for student)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students/1/courses
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.12 GET /api/students/{id}/courses — Failure: 404 Not Found (Student not found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/students/999/courses
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.13 DELETE /api/students/{id} — Failure: 404 Not Found (Student not found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/students/999

###

### 1.14 DELETE /api/students/{id} — Success: 204 No Content (Cascades and deletes student & enrollments)
# Note: First run returns 204 (deleted). Running it again returns 404 (because student 4 is already deleted).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/students/4


### ====================================================================
### 2. COURSES CONTROLLER
### ====================================================================

### 2.1 GET /api/courses/{id} — Success: 200 OK (Get course by ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.2 GET /api/courses/{id} — Failure: 404 Not Found (Course not found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/999
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.3 POST /api/courses — Success: 201 Created (Create new course)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cloud Computing & Microservices",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Building modern cloud-native systems with Docker and Kubernetes."
}

###

### 2.4 POST /api/courses — Failure: 400 Bad Request (Validation failure - invalid credits)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid Course",
  "credits": 99,
  "description": "Credits must be between 1 and 10."
}

###

### 2.5 DELETE /api/courses/{id} — Failure: 409 Conflict (Cannot delete course because it has active enrollments)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/1

###

### 2.6 DELETE /api/courses/{id} — Failure: 404 Not Found (Course not found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/999

###

### 2.7 DELETE /api/courses/{id} — Success: 204 No Content (Delete course that has NO enrollments, e.g. newly created Course 5)
# Note: First run returns 204 (No Content). Running again returns 404 (already deleted).
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/5


###

### 2.8 GET /api/courses/{id}/students — Success: 200 OK (Students enrolled in course)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/1/students
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.9 GET /api/courses/{id}/students — Failure: 404 Not Found (Course not found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/999/students
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.10 GET /api/courses/{id}/average-grade — Success: 200 OK (Average grade ignoring null grades)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/2/average-grade
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.11 GET /api/courses/{id}/average-grade — Failure: 404 Not Found (Course not found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/courses/999/average-grade
Accept: application/json


### ====================================================================
### 3. ENROLLMENTS CONTROLLER
### ====================================================================

### 3.1 POST /api/enrollments — Success: 201 Created (Enroll student in course)
# Note: First run returns 201 (Created). Running it again returns 409 Conflict (because student is already enrolled).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 2,
  "courseId": 3,
  "grade": 89
}

###

### 3.2 POST /api/enrollments — Failure: 400 Bad Request (Validation failure - invalid studentId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 0,
  "courseId": 2
}

###

### 3.3 POST /api/enrollments — Failure: 404 Not Found (Student does not exist)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 999,
  "courseId": 1
}

###

### 3.4 POST /api/enrollments — Failure: 409 Conflict (Duplicate enrollment)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": 1,
  "courseId": 1
}


### ====================================================================
### 4. ERROR HANDLING & PROBLEMDETAILS (RFC 7807)
### ====================================================================

### 4.1 GET /api/test-error — 500 Internal Server Error (ProblemDetails JSON without stack trace)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/test-error
Accept: application/json
